# Expert Instruction File Design Master Checklist

> **Goal**: Design instructions that guarantee **consistent and predictable high-quality results** for users

---

## Phase 1: Pre-Design Strategy

### Goal Definition
- [ ] **Primary Outcome**: Is the final deliverable defined in one sentence?
  - Example: "Investor-ready PRD document" / "Production-deployable code"
- [ ] **Success Criteria**: Are success criteria measurable?
  - Example: "12+ of 15 sections completed" / "Test coverage 80%+"
- [ ] **Failure Cases**: Are failure scenarios defined?
  - Example: "Halt if market size calculation fails" / "Warn on API spec conflicts"

### User Segment Analysis
- [ ] **Target User**: Is the primary user clearly defined?
  - Example: "Startup PM", "Enterprise strategy team", "Investment analyst"
- [ ] **Usage Context**: Is the usage situation defined?
  - Example: "PRD for fundraising", "Internal approval proposal", "Team sharing document"

### Constraint Identification
- [ ] **Technical constraints**: Considered LLM context window / token limits?
- [ ] **Time constraints**: Is expected work time realistic?
- [ ] **Cognitive constraints**: Is information per chunk within 7±2 items?

---

## Phase 2: Structure Design (Architecture)

### Modularity Principles

#### 2.1 Independence
- [ ] **Self-containment test**: Can each module be understood immediately if picked randomly?
- [ ] **Dependency declaration**: Are prerequisites explicitly stated?
- [ ] **Fallback strategy**: Are alternatives provided when data is missing?

#### 2.2 Cohesion
- [ ] **Single responsibility principle**: Does each section cover only one topic?
- [ ] **Grouping logic**: Are related items logically grouped?

#### 2.3 Hierarchy Design
- [ ] **Depth limit**: Maximum 4 levels (# → ## → ### → ####)
- [ ] **Width balancing**: 5-9 items per level (cognitive load optimization)
- [ ] **Symmetry**: Do items at same level have similar importance/volume?

---

### Consistency

#### 3.1 Structural Consistency
- [ ] **Template pattern**: Do all analysis sections follow the same structure?
- [ ] **Metadata uniformity**: Are evaluation criteria consistent throughout?
  ```markdown
  # Use consistently across all sections
  Impact: H (High) / M (Medium) / L (Low)
  Priority: P0 / P1 / P2
  Status: ✅ Complete / 🔄 In Progress / ❌ Not Started
  ```

#### 3.2 Naming Consistency
- [ ] **Glossary**: Are key terms defined and used consistently?
- [ ] **Verb uniformity**: Are instruction verbs consistent?

#### 3.3 Visual Consistency
- [ ] **Emoji rules**: Is emoji usage systematic?
  ```markdown
  🎯 Goal
  ⚠️ Warning
  💡 Tip
  ✅ Required
  🔄 Optional
  ```

- [ ] **Table format**: Do all tables use the same style?

---

### Scalability

#### 4.1 Version Management
- [ ] **Explicit versioning**: Is the instruction file versioned?
- [ ] **Backward compatibility**: Can previous version users migrate?

#### 4.2 Module Addition/Removal
- [ ] **Plugin structure**: Does adding new sections not affect existing ones?
- [ ] **Conditional rendering**: Can sections be enabled/disabled by mode?

#### 4.3 Customization Points
- [ ] **Variable extraction**: Are frequently changing values separated as placeholders?
- [ ] **Override capability**: Can users override defaults?

---

## Phase 3: Interface Design

### Readability

#### 5.1 Information Density Optimization
- [ ] **Scannability**: Can 70% be understood by reading titles only?
- [ ] **Table vs prose ratio**: Is table/list ratio 60%+?
- [ ] **Whitespace usage**: Is there sufficient spacing between sections?

#### 5.2 Cognitive Load Management
- [ ] **Chunk size**: Is information presented within 7±2 items at a time?
- [ ] **Progress indication**: Can users know their current position?
- [ ] **Time estimates**: Is work time specified for each section?

#### 5.3 Visual Hierarchy
- [ ] **Markdown levels**: Does `#` count reflect importance?
- [ ] **Emoji system**: Are functions distinguished?
- [ ] **Color coding**: `🟢 Go / 🟡 Review / 🔴 Block`

---

### Usability

#### 6.1 Progressive Disclosure
- [ ] **Level separation**: Is complexity separated by stages?
- [ ] **Selective detail**: Are required and optional clearly separated?

#### 6.2 Error Prevention
- [ ] **Required/optional marking**: Are required fields clear?
- [ ] **Validity rules**: Are input constraints specified?
- [ ] **Examples provided**: Do all placeholders have examples?

#### 6.3 Feedback Mechanism
- [ ] **Completeness check**: Is self-diagnosis possible?
- [ ] **Quality criteria**: Are pass criteria specified?

---

## Phase 4: Quality Assurance

### Completeness

#### 7.1 Coverage
- [ ] **Happy Path**: Is the ideal scenario 100% covered?
- [ ] **Edge Cases**: Are exception handling methods provided?
- [ ] **Negative Cases**: Are "don'ts" also specified?

#### 7.2 Coherence
- [ ] **No circular references**: No A→B→C→A dependencies?
- [ ] **Contradiction removal**: No conflicting instructions?
- [ ] **Term consistency**: Not using different names for same concept?

---

### Accuracy

#### 8.1 Fact Check
- [ ] **Numeric verification**: Are example numbers realistic?
- [ ] **Source citation**: Are claims supported by evidence?

#### 8.2 Currency
- [ ] **Time-sensitive information**: Are dates specified?
- [ ] **Deprecation warnings**: Is soon-to-be-removed content marked?

---

### Testability

#### 9.1 Verifiable Results
- [ ] **Measurable goals**: Can success be confirmed numerically?
- [ ] **Sample output**: Are correct result examples provided?

#### 9.2 Self-Diagnostic Tools
- [ ] **Checklist**: Does each section have self-check items?
- [ ] **Scoring Rubric**: Can quality be evaluated by score?

---

## Phase 5: Execution Optimization

### Speed

#### 10.1 Fast Path
- [ ] **Rapid Start**: Can core deliverable be generated quickly?
- [ ] **Templates**: Are frequently used patterns templated?

#### 10.2 Shortcuts/Automation
- [ ] **Copyable blocks**: Are frequently used tables immediately copyable?
- [ ] **Script support**: Are auto-generatable parts indicated?

---

### Maintainability

#### 11.1 Documentation
- [ ] **Design intent**: Are there comments explaining why it was made this way?
- [ ] **Change history**: Are modification reasons recorded?

#### 11.2 Refactorability
- [ ] **DRY principle**: Can duplication be removed?
- [ ] **Separability**: Does it work if only parts are extracted?

---

## Phase 6: Meta Quality

### Learning Curve

#### 12.1 Usage Guide
- [ ] **Clear starting point**: Is it specified where to start?
- [ ] **Difficulty indication**: Is complexity of each section specified?

#### 12.2 Progressive Mastery
- [ ] **Improvement path**: Is continuous improvement method suggested?

---

### Adaptability

#### 13.1 Domain Independence
- [ ] **Universality**: Is it applicable to other industries?
- [ ] **Customization guide**: Are industry-specific variation methods explained?

#### 13.2 Collaboration Friendliness
- [ ] **Role division**: Can it be divided for team work?
- [ ] **Mergeable**: Can multiple people's results be combined?

---

